-- R22 - Credit filter line on equity cards and the BOOK CHECK; Fed-cycle stage line on USD and UST cards; tags for a
-- weekly cut, no gate change (both Macro Takeaways digests).
-- Source: thread "Compare macro book with our trading rules"; the owner's yes of 16 Nov 2026.
-- Proposed 16 Nov 2026 with dash.propose_rule and put in force the same day on the owner's word.
-- Text below is byte-identical to the DB row (body md5 f0947d3d77e01457d1e1e35e9a161a7a).
-- Data: section H of the market pack (scripts/marketpack/marketpack.py); META keys "credit" and "cycle" in _shared/parse.ts.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Credit filter line on equity cards and the BOOK CHECK; Fed-cycle stage line on USD and UST cards; tags for a weekly cut, no gate change", "body": "CREDIT AND CYCLE LINES (thread \"Compare macro book with our trading rules\", owner's yes 16 Nov 2026). Two printed evidence lines from the market pack's section H, taken from Willer and Saunders, Trading Global Macro Markets (Wiley 2026): a VIX spike carries information for equities only when high-yield spreads have widened over six months, and credit turns before equities (ch. 3, 11); rates and dollar trades have a prior that depends on where the Fed is in its cycle (ch. 5, 13). This rule prints the two lines and tags the cards so the weekly review can cut by them. It changes no gate, no fill, no exit and no size, and neither line is by itself a reason to raise or lower p. Applies in both books.\n\n1. READ. Section H of market_pack_latest holds one CREDIT line (HY OAS level, 1-month and 6-month change, 3-year percentile, VIX and its 250-day z-score, and a state: confirmed, unconfirmed, calm-wider or calm) and one CYCLE line (Fed target, EFFR, the last move, what fed funds futures price 3, 6 and 12 months out, a stage: pre-hike, hiking, late-hiking, hold, pre-cut, easing or late-easing, and the book prior for that stage). Copy both from the pack; never rebuild them from the web. If section H is missing or says \"not available\", print \"CREDIT: n/a\" or \"CYCLE: n/a\" and write the tag as \"-\".\n\n2. CREDIT, where it prints. (a) On every NEW card whose proxy is an equity index, an equity-index future or ETF, ^VIX, or a credit ETF (HYG, LQD, EMB): directly after the TREND line (R21), \"CREDIT: HY OAS <x.xx>% (6m <±n>bp), VIX z <±x.x>, <state>\". (b) In the BOOK CHECK, one line with the same text. (c) A NEW long equity card written while the state is confirmed, and a NEW short equity card whose p reason is a VIX spike while the state is unconfirmed, names the state in its case against. META gains, after the trend key, \"· credit <state>\".\n\n3. CYCLE, where it prints. (a) In the macro section's rates paragraph, once: the CYCLE line as the pack prints it. (b) On every NEW card whose proxy is a UST yield or bond future, a SOFR or fed funds future, DXY or a USD pair: directly after the TREND line, \"CYCLE: <stage>, futures <±n>bp in 12m; book prior <prior>; card is <with / against / no prior>\". A card against the book prior names in its p reason what makes this cycle different. META gains, after the trend key, \"· cycle <stage>\".\n\n4. WEEKLY CUT. The weekly review adds two cuts of closed cards once ten carry a tag: equity and credit cards by credit state x side (long/short), and rates and USD cards by cycle stage x with/against the prior: n, wins, targets, stops, cum R as booked, average stated p. Until dash-ingest stores the two keys, the review joins a card's opened date to /mnt/project-files/marketpack/credit_cycle_history.csv (one row a day, written by the pack).\n\n5. DECISION. At 20 closed tagged cards in either cut, or on 28 February 2027, whichever comes first, the weekly review proposes for that cut: keep as disclosure, drop the line, or a payoff haircut in the form of R09 on the bucket that lost. Until then no card is rejected, haircut or sized on these lines.\n\n6. FIRST RUN. Open and pending cards get no tag and no restatement. The trade block's footer gains \"credit <state> · cycle <stage>\".", "rationale": "Owner said yes on 16 Nov 2026 to the two cheapest of the parked ideas from the book comparison, as print-only lines. The data is one FRED daily series each for HY OAS, the Fed target and EFFR, plus VIX and fed funds futures already reachable from the pack. Our own record cannot test either yet (about a dozen closed equity cards, and six weeks inside one cycle stage), so the rule only prints, tags and sets a decision point.", "evidence": "Book: Willer and Saunders 2026, ch. 3 and 11 (a VIX +2 sigma exit adds no information ratio unless HY spreads have widened over six months; credit spreads trough about 12 months before recessions, equities about 6), ch. 5 and 13 (payers from 3 months before the first hike until the last hike; receivers around the last hike and 3 months before the first cut; the easy receiving trade ends with the last cut; USD falls about 4% into the first cut and is sideways after). Own record: none yet; this rule creates it. Pack section H built and tested 16 Nov 2026.", "revert_if": "Revert if section H fails to build on 3 or more mornings in a week, or a weekly review finds the state or stage misread on 2 or more cards, or the step costs the 08:15 SGT landing on 2 or more days with no other failure to explain it. The decision of item 5 is taken once per cut.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2027-02-28", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
